          IDENT  CPUTEXT
          ENTRY  START
*         COUNTS THE LETTERS OF A MESSAGE AND COPIES IT TO A BUFFER.
*
*         THE TEXT IS IN DISPLAY CODE: 6 BITS PER CHARACTER, 10
*         CHARACTERS PER WORD (A = 01B, Z = 32B, 0 = 33B, BLANK = 55B).
*         EACH CHARACTER IS EXTRACTED BY ROTATION (LX) AND MASK (MX).
*
*         JOB UNDER THE MINI-SYSTEM (SYSTEM MODE): THE COPY OF THE
*         MESSAGE AND THE COUNTS ARE PRINTED ON THE LINE PRINTER
*         (WRITEC); THE COUNTS GO TO THE DAYFILE AND THE CONSOLE
*         (MESSAGE).
*
START     SB1    1           B1 = 1
          SB3    B0          B3 = WORD INDEX
          SX7    B0          X7 = NUMBER OF LETTERS
          MX0    54          X0 = MASK OF THE UPPER 54 BITS
WORD      SA1    B3+MSGTEXT  X1 = NEXT WORD
          ZR     X1,DONE     ZERO WORD: END OF MESSAGE
          BX6    X1
          SA6    B3+BUFFER   COPY THE WORD
          SB4    10          10 CHARACTERS PER WORD
CHR       LX1    6           NEXT CHARACTER TO THE BOTTOM
          BX2    -X0*X1      X2 = LOWER 6 BITS OF X1
          SX3    X2-1        LETTER IF 1 <= C <= 32B
          NG     X3,NEXTCH
          SX3    X2-1R0      C - 33B
          PL     X3,NEXTCH
          SX7    X7+1        ONE MORE LETTER
NEXTCH    SB4    B4-B1
          NZ     B4,CHR
          SB3    B3+B1       NEXT WORD
          EQ     WORD
*
DONE      SA7    LETTERS     NUMBER OF LETTERS
          SX6    B3
          SA6    WORDS       NUMBER OF WORDS
*
*         PRINT THE COPY AND THE COUNTS. THE MESSAGE STARTS WITH A
*         BLANK: THE FIRST CHARACTER OF A PRINTED LINE IS THE
*         CARRIAGE CONTROL (BLANK = SINGLE SPACE).
*
          WRITEC OUTPUT,BUFFER
          SA1    LETTERS
          CDD                X6 = DECIMAL DIGITS
          SA6    LINE1+2
          WRITEC OUTPUT,LINE1
          MESSAGE LINE1      DAYFILE AND CONSOLE
          SA1    WORDS
          CDD
          SA6    LINE2+2
          WRITEC OUTPUT,LINE2
          MESSAGE LINE2
          WRITER OUTPUT      WRITE THE BUFFER TO THE PRINTER
          ENDRUN
*
MSGTEXT   DIS    ,* HELLO FROM THE CDC 6600, THE FIRST SUPERCOMPUTER.*
          CON    0           TERMINATING ZERO WORD
LINE1     DIS    2, LETTERS IN TEXT   =
          BSSZ   1           NUMBER
          CON    0           END OF LINE
LINE2     DIS    2, WORDS OF 10 CHARS =
          BSSZ   1
          CON    0
LETTERS   BSS    1
WORDS     BSS    1
BUFFER    BSSZ   10
*
OUTPUT    FILEC  BUF,BUFL    FILE OUTPUT = LINE PRINTER
BUFL      EQU    101B
BUF       BSS    BUFL
          END    START
